{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc-rule-induction", "file": "references/uniform-row-periodicity.md", "content": "# Uniform-row grids and periodic completion

When each input row is a single repeated color and some rows are blank/background, demos may encode a vertical sequence rather than a local object transformation. Record each row's output color by index, then test candidate period and phase against every observed non-background input stripe. Verify the completed cycle against the whole output, including boundaries. An unchanged demo may already contain a complete cycle; it does not prove that all inputs should remain unchanged.

